X86 SB+pmap-none
(*
 * #350 - baseline / liveness of the harness: neither thread fences.  Plain SB.
 * Expected verdict: Sometimes  ->  confirms the catastrophe state is expressible
 * and reachable, so a "Never" in sb-pmap-both is a real proof and not a typo that
 * made the bad state unreachable by construction (a vacuous pass).
 *
 * See sb-pmap-both.litmus for the full mapping and modeling notes.
 *)
{ pte=0; cpus=0; }
 P0             | P1             ;
 MOV [pte],$1   | MOV [cpus],$1  ;
 MOV EAX,[cpus] | MOV EAX,[pte]  ;
exists (0:EAX=0 /\ 1:EAX=0)
